commit 78fb865b69552c5e383bbaddc85cbe01bca7f4a6
Author: Matthijs van Henten <[REDACTED-EMAIL]>
Date:   Mon Sep 28 06:04:02 2026 +0000

    feat: numeric stroke width on every object

    Every object and live ink frame carries width, a finite number of screen
    px at the native level from 0.5 to 96, next to size, which now holds the
    nearest enum. Objects written before width lack it; readers derive it
    from PENCIL_PX[size], and the codec always writes it. The palette gets a
    width slider and presets from 0.5 to 96 px; the quick-bar sizes set width
    too. The smoke draws at 1 px and 60 px and checks their ink keeps its
    order after a reload.

    Closes #22

